      "side": 1,
      "message": "Switching to longValue() now accepts chunk sizes above Integer.MAX_VALUE, but ResponseBodyOutputStream later calls maxChunkSize.intValue(), which goes negative, so every HTTP/1.1 response throws in Open\u0027s constructor and is only logged by ServerRequestExecutor.writeResponse. Could we also reject values above Integer.MAX_VALUE here, and change responseChunkSizeUsesUnsignedRange to expect rejection instead of accepting 4294967295?",
      "revId": "12f90e66395ae19e8872eebb8469587caa074d6c",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
